WEBVTT

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:05.980
In the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit, Amen!

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:13.860
The reading from the Sinaxadion for September 17th, on which we commemorate the Holy Virgin

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:22.690
martyrs, faith, hope and love and their mother, Sophia.

00:00:22.690 --> 00:00:30.610
On the 17th of the month, we celebrate the memory of the Holy martyrs, Pistis, Elpis,

00:00:30.610 --> 00:00:36.340
Agape, and their mother, Sophia.

00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:45.740
These Holy martyrs dwelt in Italy in the reign of Hadrian in the years 117 through 138.

00:00:45.740 --> 00:00:51.620
They came of a rich and devout family, and their mother, Sophia, brought them up in the

00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:58.180
faith, hope and charity of the names she had given them.

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:04.220
The Lord of their admirable manner of life reached the Emperor, who, hearing they were

00:01:04.220 --> 00:01:09.580
in Rome, sent soldiers to bring them before him.

00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:15.060
Considering their tender years, he was amazed at how steadfast in the faith Sophia's daughters

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:21.700
were, and thinking it was only by supporting one another, that they were able to hold their

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:23.740
own against him.

00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:28.700
He put them to the question separately.

00:01:28.700 --> 00:01:33.940
Pistis, who was twelve years old, was brought in first.

00:01:33.940 --> 00:01:42.060
She boldly dismissed the tyrants' flatteries and deprecated his shameless deeds and vain plots

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:44.900
against the Christians.

00:01:44.900 --> 00:01:53.940
The infuriated Emperor had her stripped, mercilessly beaten, and her breasts torn off.

00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:59.980
Wentz milk, not blood, flowed forth.

00:01:59.980 --> 00:02:07.660
The other tortures she endured were to no avail, for she was protected by the power of God.

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:15.260
When at last they came to strike off her head, Sophia encouraged her to accept with joy,

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:19.860
the death that would unite her to Christ.

00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:24.380
Elpys, who was ten years old, was brought in next.

00:02:24.380 --> 00:02:32.260
Confessing Christ, as steadfastly as her sister, she was beaten and cast into a raging furnace,

00:02:32.260 --> 00:02:39.420
but its fire went out on touching her, in whom love of God burnt with a fiercer flame

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:42.340
than material fire.

00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:49.700
After many other tortures, she too died by the sword, giving thanks to God.

00:02:49.700 --> 00:02:56.980
Agapi, the third of the sisters, was then summoned before the Emperor, whom anger had

00:02:56.980 --> 00:02:58.460
mattened.

00:02:58.460 --> 00:03:04.980
She was only nine years old, but of the same steadfast mind as her sisters.

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:12.300
She was hung on a gallows and chained so tightly that her limbs were broken by the bonds.

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:20.140
She was then thrown into a furnace, from which she was delivered by an angel, and finally

00:03:20.140 --> 00:03:21.940
beheaded.

00:03:21.940 --> 00:03:28.180
Sophia rejoiced in spirit to see her daughters so gloriously making their way to the abodes

00:03:28.180 --> 00:03:34.140
of the righteous, but overwhelmed by earthly sorrow.

00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:42.760
She gave back her soul to God a few days later, at their tomb, through the prayers of our

00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:50.000
Holy Father's, O Lord, Jesus Christ our God, have mercy on us and save us.
